target: internal/evidence/evidence.go
verify: go test ./internal/evidence/ -count=1 -run 'TestPendingReportsListsEveryFileInPathOrder'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    `looper record pending` must list every file runlog.py's glob did, in path order, so that a stray one is still named on stderr instead of sitting unseen in its run dir. Filtering by evidence.ValidRunID looks like hardening and is a silent divergence: the first version of PendingReports did exactly that and also sorted by id.
--- old
	sort.Strings(files)
--- new
	sort.Strings(files)
	for i := len(files) - 1; i >= 0; i-- {
		if !ValidRunID(filepath.Base(filepath.Dir(files[i]))) {
			files = append(files[:i], files[i+1:]...)
		}
	}
